infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Conditional type vs discriminated union + if
  desc The senior breakpoint — does the return type vary with the input, or do you only need one runtime decision?
  compares
    - label Conditional type: type varies with the argument
      children
        - label Return type tracks the input automatically
          desc One signature models overload-like returns — Awaited, unwrap
        - label Zero runtime cost
          desc Pure type-level; nothing reaches the bundle
        - label Bills come due at compile time and in errors
          desc Distribution can near the 100,000-member union cap; the tooltip shows the whole nested conditional, not a name
    - label Discriminated union + plain if: one runtime decision
      children
        - label Cheaper to read and to compile
          desc No per-member distribution, no instantiation blowup
        - label Error message a teammate can act on
          desc Points at a value, not an unresolved type
        - label Pays one branch at runtime
          desc The decision costs a real if at execution time, not type-checker time
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
